{"surface": "event", "title": "The Fed's rate is 4.75% or higher after its April 28, 2027 meeting", "html": "<div class=\"ev ws\"><div class=\"evh\"><h2 class=\"title\">The Fed&#x27;s rate is 4.75% or higher after its April 28, 2027 meeting</h2><p class=\"facts\"><span>The decision on Apr 28, 2027</span><span class=\"sep\">·</span><span class=\"src\">Known from Federal Reserve FOMC statements</span></p><div class=\"hds\"><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"definition\"><summary>Definition</summary><div class=\"hdb text\"><p>The upper bound of the federal funds target range stands at 4.75% or higher after the FOMC meeting that ends April 28, 2027: at least three more quarter-point rises from today&#x27;s 3.75%-4.00% across the December, January, March and April meetings. April&#x27;s is the last meeting inside the horizon.</p></div></details><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"notes\"><summary>Rationale</summary><div class=\"hdb\"><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:9\" data-note=\"note:9\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"If the Fed raises in December, January and March the rate is already 4.75% after March; it stays at or above that unless April brings a cut. Polymarket&#x27;s April-decision market puts a cut at about 12% unconditionally, and a cut one meeting after three straight rises is less likely than that, so 0.92.\"><p>If the Fed raises in December, January and March the rate is already 4.75% after March; it stays at or above that unless April brings a cut. Polymarket&#x27;s April-decision market puts a cut at about 12% unconditionally, and a cut one meeting after three straight rises is less likely than that, so 0.92.</p></div></div><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:10\" data-note=\"note:10\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"Without three straight rises, 4.75% by April needs two rises by March and another in April, or a half-point step. Polymarket&#x27;s parlay puts two-of-three paths (Hike-Hike-Pause, Hike-Pause-Hike) at about 0.53 of all paths, 0.80 of the paths that are not Hike-Hike-Hike; an April rise is priced near 0.24. 0.80 x 0.24 is 0.19.\"><p>Without three straight rises, 4.75% by April needs two rises by March and another in April, or a half-point step. Polymarket&#x27;s parlay puts two-of-three paths (Hike-Hike-Pause, Hike-Pause-Hike) at about 0.53 of all paths, 0.80 of the paths that are not Hike-Hike-Hike; an April rise is priced near 0.24. 0.80 x 0.24 is 0.19.</p></div></div><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:84\" data-note=\"note:84\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"An AI bust is a growth and financial-conditions shock, and Fed staff called AI-related demand &#x27;a material source of inflation risk&#x27;. If the build-out breaks, the Fed has less reason to keep raising, so three or more further rises by April become less likely than otherwise: 0.25 against 0.44 overall. The bust can arrive after rises already made, which is why it is not lower.\"><p>An AI bust is a growth and financial-conditions shock, and Fed staff called AI-related demand &#x27;a material source of inflation risk&#x27;. If the build-out breaks, the Fed has less reason to keep raising, so three or more further rises by April become less likely than otherwise: 0.25 against 0.44 overall. The bust can arrive after rises already made, which is why it is not lower.</p></div></div></div></details></div></div><div class=\"strip\" data-count=\"8\" style=\"--cols:5\"><div class=\"sf first\" data-k=\"fig:Forecast\"><span class=\"lab\">Forecast</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:12\"><span class=\"n v\">44.2%</span></a></span><a class=\"cap go calc\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:12\">How it’s set →</a></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Market range\"><span class=\"lab\">Market range</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:interval:prop:12\"><span class=\"n v\">21.0%–85.0%</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Market\"><span class=\"lab\">Market</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:price:market:kalshi